What is the value of $n$ in the equation $4n - 2 = 3n + 19$?
Steps: Subtracting $3n$ from both sides, we have \begin{align*}
4n - 2 &= 3n + 19 \\
4n - 3n - 2 &= 3n - 3n + 19 \\
n - 2 &= 19.
\end{align*} Adding 2 to both sides, we have \begin{align*}
n - 2 + 2 &= 19 + 2 \\
n &= \boxed{21}.
\end{align*}  ~ilp
