r&=\frac{a+b}{2} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad 2r&=a+b
\end{align*}We also have that \begin{align*}
a^2-b^2&=(a+b)(a-b) \\
&=2r(a-b)
\end{align*}Plugging this into our expression for the slope of line $AB$, we have \begin{align*}
