We have that \begin{align*}
\|\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}\|&=\sqrt{\|\mathbf{c}\|^2 - 2 \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{c} + \|\mathbf{a}\|^2}\\
&=\sqrt{\|\mathbf{c}\|^2 - 2\|\mathbf{c} \times \mathbf{a}\| + \|\mathbf{a}\|^2}\\
&=\sqrt{\|\mathbf{c}\|^2 - 2 \|\mathbf{b}\| + \|\mathbf{a}\|^2}
\end{align*}By the triangle inequality, we have that \begin{align*}
\|\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}\|&=\sqrt{\|\mathbf{c}\|^2 - 2 \|\mathbf{b}\| + \|\mathbf{a}\|^2}\\
&=\sqrt{\|\mathbf{c}\|^2 + \|\mathbf{a}\|^2 - 2 \|\mathbf{b}\|}\\
&\geq \sqrt{\|\mathbf{b}\|^2 + \|\mathbf{a}\|^2 - 2 \|\mathbf{b}\|}\\
&=\sqrt{3^2 + 2^2 - 2 \cdot 3}\\
&=\sqrt{9+4-6}\\
&=\sqrt{7}
\end{align*}The minimum value of $\|\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}\|$ is $\sqrt{7}$. Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{\sqrt{7}}$.

